    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - LoRA Toolkit (the fourth video tutorial)\n\nBulle d'Encre (huggingface.co/DeVilDoNia/Bulle-d-Encre) is SFT with 30% of Base in layers 24-29, plus\nTurbo 8-steps v1.0 at 0.5 and the author's style LoRA at 0.8. Its recipe shows in the Metadata Reader.\n\nAs it opens, a run gives the rebuilt base alone (the Block Merger) at 15 steps, CFG 2.5, euler / simple.\n1. Unmute the Load Diffusion Model (Bulle d'Encre), the LoRA Extractor and its text preview (Ctrl+M)\n   and run: models/loras/bulle_extracted.safetensors, rank 64, 252 MB, 97% of the difference, about 100 s.\n   Then mute them again and press R so the lists see the new file.\n2. Switch the Multi-LoRA on: the base + the extracted LoRA gives Bulle d'Encre's look back.\n   Turn the Turbo row on (0.5) and set the KSampler to 8 steps, CFG 1: the same scene and look.\n   Each row folds out a weight per group of 6 layers: here layers 24-35 carry most of the style.\n3. Unmute the LoRA Merger and run: one file, 255 MB, the same maths as the two rows within 0.24%.\n   Then the LoRA Resize at rank 32: 126 MB, within the noise of the merged file's images.\n4. Pick bulle_turbo_r32 in the Metadata Reader: the whole chain back to Bulle d'Encre.\n\nFiles are saved at the root of models/loras. Measurements: tools/RESULTS.md in the HaDeS MOSS Suite."
